{"name":"Antique Gold","hex":"#b59e5f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"antique","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having existed in ancient times, descended from antiquity; used especially in reference to Greece and Rome.","Belonging to former times, not modern, out of date, old-fashioned."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In general, anything very old; specifically:\n An old object perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance.","An old object perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antique"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"},{"title":"Antique","blocks":[{"text":"An antique is an item perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance, and often defined as at least 100 years old, although the term is often used loosely to describe any object that is old. An antique is usually an item that is collected or desirable because of its age, beauty, rarity, condition, utility, personal emotional connection, or other unique features. It is an object that represents a previous era or time period in human history. Vintage and collectible are used to describe items that are old, but do not meet the 100-year criterion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/06_Restoration_of_gilded_mirror_in_Muzeum_Gornoslaskie%2C_Bytom%2C_Poland_-_furniture_restorer_working.jpg/330px-06_Restoration_of_gilded_mirror_in_Muzeum_Gornoslaskie%2C_Bytom%2C_Poland_-_furniture_restorer_working.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antique","wikidata":"Q472760"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg/500px-Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg/500px-Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMultiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse